{%- comment -%}
  Preserve Shopify's default crawler rules, then provide explicit access rules for
  answer-engine crawlers without exposing cart, checkout, customer, or search URLs.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Whitespace control here is load-bearing and easy to break.

  Shopify's default groups render one directive per value - "User-agent: *",
  "Disallow: /cart" and so on - with no trailing newline of their own. The line
  breaks come from the template. Until 2026-09-14 every output tag in this loop
  used {{- x -}}, whose trailing hyphen strips the newline after it, so all of
  Shopify's default rules collapsed onto a single unparseable line and every one
  of them was silently void.

  {{- x }} is correct: strip the indent before the value, keep the newline after
  it. That is Shopify's own documented pattern. Do not add the trailing hyphen.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% for group in robots.default_groups %}
  {{- group.user_agent }}
  {% for rule in group.rules %}
    {{- rule }}
  {% endfor %}
  {%- if group.sitemap != blank %}
    {{- group.sitemap }}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{%- comment -%}
  POLICY: answer engines are allowed on purpose. Blocking GPTBot removes NUR from
  ChatGPT retrieval; blocking Google-Extended removes it from Gemini grounding.
  For a brand nobody searches by name yet, being retrievable is worth more than
  being withheld. If that is ever reversed, reverse it deliberately and say why
  here - do not "harden" this list by reflex.

  ChatGPT-User (the browsing agent), Google-Extended, Applebot-Extended and
  Bingbot were previously unnamed and fell through to the permissive "*" group.
  They are listed now so the policy is explicit rather than incidental.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign nur_search_crawlers = 'OAI-SearchBot|GPTBot|ChatGPT-User|PerplexityBot|ClaudeBot|Applebot|Applebot-Extended|Google-Extended|Bingbot' | split: '|' -%}
{%- for crawler in nur_search_crawlers %}
User-agent: {{ crawler }}
Allow: /
Disallow: /admin
Disallow: /cart
Disallow: /carts
Disallow: /checkout
Disallow: /checkouts
Disallow: /account
Disallow: /orders
Disallow: /search
Disallow: /recommendations/products
Disallow: /tools/

{%- endfor -%}
Sitemap: {{ shop.url }}/sitemap.xml
